{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1520613-what-is-the-invictus","id":1520613,"title":"What is the Invictus?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-14T14:49:33-07:00","id":1520613,"title":"What is the Invictus?","content":"I swear I'm not snide. I just don't get the Invictus, especially what they do when they are not in power. <br /> <br /> The other Covenants are defined rather easily. The Lancea et Sanctum has their whole &quot;be God's monster&quot;: the Circle of the Crone has their religion and possibly links to other supernatural phenomena, the Ordo Dracul has the who quest for transcendance and strange experiments, even the Carthians I get in that they are trying different political organizations for vampires. <br /> <br /> The Invictus is the only one I don't get. They have a clear internal organization based on patronage. They focus on the Masquerade so I suppose I could lean into that and make them the &quot;mortal business&quot; Covenant. That's the vibe I get from their Secrets of the Covenant chapter. <br /> <br /> Am I missing something? The 1st edition Covenant book spends most of its page count on the internal hierarchy and seem to present them as aristocrats basically ploting against each other but that doesn't seem to sustain a Covenant, especially when they are not in power in a given city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T15:15:35-07:00","id":1520618,"title":"","content":"The Invictus is basically &quot;Camarilla Lite&quot;, at least when Requiem first started. It's since morphed over the years, of course/<br /> <br /> The covenants of Requiem each sync up with a different faction of Masquerade, at least in the 1e corebook and the early Requiem materials from 1e.<br /> <br /> Invictus - Camarilla<br /> Carthians - Anarchs<br /> Lancea Sanctum - Revised-era Sabbat with some elements of the Salubri Warriors from Dark Ages<br /> Circle of the Crone - 2e-era Sabbat<br /> Ordo Dracul - Tremere Pyramid with elements of the Tzimisce Road of Metamorphosis<br /> Belial's Brood - Baali, Infernalists/Path of Evil Revelations<br /> VII - 1e Assamites, 1e &quot;Black Hand&quot; Sabbat, Revised-era Inconnu","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T15:59:21-07:00","id":1520622,"title":"","content":"The Invictus are competent. If you need the Masquerade maintained and it needs to be done right, you can rely on the Invictus. If a hunter is causing problems you can trust the Invictus. If you need an oath over seen, or if you need a job done but want an oath binding the person who does it the Invictus got you covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T16:44:02-07:00","id":1520631,"title":"","content":"The Invictus are, simply put, the aristocratic masters of the night. Whereas the other Covenants are focused on mystical and or historical pursuits along with societal upheaval, the Invictus are concerned chiefly with gaining temporal power and running the all night society as they always have.<br /> <br /> In other words, it's about control. They have their hands in everything, and unlike the carthians, it's not to manipulate for a revolution or to further a social experiments, it's simply to have power and to maintain that power. It's so they can do as they please and dictate what others do, whether they wish to or not<br /> <br /> But that's not just it. You say it's the Masquerade that they have, but that's a creation of the Lancea Et Sanctum. And all the factions utilize it, one way or the other. The Invictus does specialize in it, yes, but moreso, they keep to an even bigger lie; the lie that they aren't monsters. More than any other faction, save perhaps the Lancea Et Sanctum (and even then, that's only when you ignore WHAT they dress up vampires as), the Invictus maintains an aura of nobility and a pretense of human social conventions to the vampiric condition. They may be parasites who have the police, the mayor, the judge, and your local plumber in thrall, but they will do so under the guise of a ruler reigning over a kingdom and doing what's good for his subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T17:39:42-07:00","id":1520634,"title":"","content":"The Invictus preserves the Masquerade, preserves their hierarchy, and preserves itself. The Conspiracy of Silence is the vampiric equivalent of Deviant's Web of Pain or Demon's layers of social Infrastructure, acting to build a power base and deepen the security (in various senses) of the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Other vampires may engage in conspiracy, protect the secrets of vampires and vampirism, and subvert mortal institutions to their will but the Invictus makes all of that their <i>operational focus.</i> Their job is to make the status quo benefit themselves and their allies and then keep that status quo going for as long as they can (or control for what it changes to if they can't). They make sure the Rack doesn't run dry from a sudden change in curfew and zoning laws. They keep the elders' coffers filled when a bad fiscal quarter comes home to roost. They make diplomatic overtures to the occultically-inclined covenants for their expertise when something magical needs dealt with. They <i>make the machine run</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T19:44:32-07:00","id":1520639,"title":"","content":"I once described the Invictus as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1463758-if-the-invictus-are-caught-trying-to-oust-a-non-invictus-prince-what-then?p=1463847#post1463847\">the organization that aspires to be the ocean that the other covenants pass over as storms,</a> the one whose right to rule is expressed by virtue of always being the one doing something about the domain. They're a Neo-feudal Men in Black, the unholy technocratic fiefdoms of capitalistic rule, occult taxation, and blood rule in the truest sense of the words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T20:37:23-07:00","id":1520642,"title":"","content":"To add another analogy that might be a bit more on &quot;what do the Invictus do, especially when not in power,&quot; in a more partical sense:<br /> <br /> They're lawyers, and importantly all members of a few small well connected firms (read or watch The Firm, or the Devil's Advocate for the kind of firms they tend to build up). They have contract lawyers and notaries to put everything down in a binding way. Everyone is an expert in a kind of law, not just to best serve their clients, but to grow the power of their firm. Knowing the law better, and knowing the people that operate the law better, lets them lawyer with more and more power. Even if you're powerful, when you have legal matters, you find the best lawyers you can to fix your problems. You probably keep the best firm on retainer so other people can't use them against you (think about the kind of social clout that the Invictus want: even as servants they're indispensable enough nobody can afford to let them support someone else).<br /> <br /> When they're in power, ex-firm members are high powered judges/justices and politicians too (look at how many powerful politicians have been/are lawyers) on top of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T02:43:54-07:00","id":1520655,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers. <br /> <br /> To give some context I storytell a campaign where the domain is led by the Ordo Dracul, two of the players are Dragons, the last Invictus. Your answers make me think that what I had planned ie: The Invictus of the city is concerned by ensuring mortal prey is plentiful, Masquerade is maintained, and being the anti-Hunter Covenant work. They are also the Covenant more involved in mortal interactions as part of their raison d'\u00eatre is to subvert infrastructures to vampiric needs. <br /> <br /> Where I'm perhaps wrongly surprised is I thought the last part, being the &quot;mortals politics&quot; Covenant, in that the Invictus is meddling in mortal affairs, was the Carthian's schtick in 1st edition. The Invictus covenant book focuses more on vampire-vampire interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T04:37:30-07:00","id":1520657,"title":"","content":"Both covenants meddle in mortal affairs. Invictus might whisper in Donald Trump's ear, while Carthians might influence a BLM protest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T08:29:37-07:00","id":1520678,"title":"","content":"Both the Carthian &amp; Invictus will involve themselves in mortal political affairs at some point. The key difference is whom they go with as the Invictus might place themselves in Mayor's, Governor's, Premier's and Senior Executives of large corporations to ensure there interests are met and the status quo is maintained. Where as the Carthians may influence Unions, Activists, and Blue Collar workers.<br /> <br /> The Invictus wants things to stay the way that favours them and Carthians want to remake there society into a different direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-15-2023, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T08:31:33-07:00","id":1520680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1520613-what-is-the-invictus?p=1520655#post1520655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> To give some context I storytell a campaign where the domain is led by the Ordo Dracul, two of the players are Dragons, the last Invictus. Your answers make me think that what I had planned ie: The Invictus of the city is concerned by ensuring mortal prey is plentiful, Masquerade is maintained, and being the anti-Hunter Covenant work. They are also the Covenant more involved in mortal interactions as part of their raison d'\u00eatre is to subvert infrastructures to vampiric needs.<br /> <br /> Where I'm perhaps wrongly surprised is I thought the last part, being the &quot;mortals politics&quot; Covenant, in that the Invictus is meddling in mortal affairs, was the Carthian's schtick in 1st edition. The Invictus covenant book focuses more on vampire-vampire interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make no mistake, the Invictus are VERY embedded in vampire-vampire politics. That's what the tangled web of Oaths is for, and ultimately all their mortal mortal manipulations are to ensure the smooth running of the all night society<br /> <br /> The Carthians, however, are concerned with upheaval of undead political body. Ultimately, the Invictus have running machine, and that's what matters. It runs, hat else is there to worry about? The carthians, though? They want to break that machine and start anew, and that requires swaying (or staking) the hearts and minds of the Kindred. Messing with mortal affairs is a means to shake up the danse macabre or to learn how better to imitate their ways","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T11:31:47-07:00","id":1520691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1520613-what-is-the-invictus?p=1520655#post1520655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where I'm perhaps wrongly surprised is I thought the last part, being the &quot;mortals politics&quot; Covenant, in that the Invictus is meddling in mortal affairs, was the Carthian's schtick in 1st edition. The Invictus covenant book focuses more on vampire-vampire interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might've been more true in First Edition, but Second Edition's clarifications kind of shifts the balance. The Carthians are <i>aware</i> of the power of manipulating the kine to action, but their central concern is revolutionizing vrykosocietal forms, not human ones, and as such are a vampires politics covenant that uses mortal politics to mess with the other covenants. The Invictus, having had their role as the Conspiracy of Silence firmly established, are interested in maintaining the vrykosocietal status quo on both the Kindred and kine fronts, so their interests in vampiric and mortal politics is more balanced as they keep the whole together. Arguably they too use mortal politics to the ends of vampire politics, but theirs is a more holisitic view.<br /> <br /> I mentioned, in a thread about vampiric morality, that of the five main covenants, the Invictus are the ones most institutionally interested in the upkeep, wellbeing, and care of humanity, even as that means corrupting the shit out of their structures and systems-it's that holistic view that where that comes from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-15-2023, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T07:47:20-07:00","id":1520768,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s an old UK comedy called Yes Minster, it\u2019s basically how the Invictus deal with any ruler they disagree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T10:00:47-07:00","id":1520894,"title":"","content":"I feel as though when it comes to politics, the Invictus is more about providing an outlet and an appeal for vampires in terms of getting to be people who have a strong say in the decisions, rather than necessarily using the decisions to achieve an agenda. The gratification of getting to know that you're in the room where it happens.<br /> <br /> Although perhaps occasionally there are vampires who had particular agendas that carry over from when they were human, and they see how the Invictus provides the framework to acquire the leverage to see them through.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I feel as though &quot;preserving the status quo&quot; is too non-descript a way to describe the motivations of a conspiratorial group, because it excludes characters who can be highly motivated, implies a setting that lacks dynamism that is hard to feel true to life, and implies that a lot of the most objectionable things about the world are not depressingly resilient.<br /> <br /> Besides, is it not interesting to imagine scenarios in which vampires of the Invictus conspired to make a contribution to some noteworthy worldwide change because it actually made things more suitable for them? Indeed, to have a setting in which one can participate in some kind of proactive project towards that end?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T19:33:11-07:00","id":1520919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1520613-what-is-the-invictus?p=1520894#post1520894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I feel as though &quot;preserving the status quo&quot; is too non-descript a way to describe the motivations of a conspiratorial group, because it excludes characters who can be highly motivated, implies a setting that lacks dynamism that is hard to feel true to life, and implies that a lot of the most objectionable things about the world are not depressingly resilient.<br /> <br /> Besides, is it not interesting to imagine scenarios in which vampires of the Invictus conspired to make a contribution to some noteworthy worldwide change because it actually made things more suitable for them? Indeed, to have a setting in which one can participate in some kind of proactive project towards that end?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the book says, you have to change an awful lot to stay the same. The little economy-destabilizing wager in the Invictus chapter of Secrets of the Covenants is just one example of the kind of constant aggregate scramble the Conspiracy of Silence is operating under to make sure they stay on top of things.<br /> <br /> Nobody who's going to wake up forty nights from now is so complacent as to think the status quo is secure when that status quo includes &quot;vampires need to keep themselves from being discovered by humans and have very limited passive means of hiding evidence of their status as supernatural actors compared to most other monsters.&quot; If nothing else, the bodies need disposed of and the patterns need changed often enough that nobody puts together a conclusive picture without being in on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T10:55:31-07:00","id":1520961,"title":"","content":"In regards to the Status Quo I should have been more detailed in the fact that the Invictus would spend lots of time to ensure that the Masquerade remains intact and by being near the people and places of true power would be the best solution &amp; nudging them into areas that serve there interests the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T11:38:46-07:00","id":1520965,"title":"","content":"In my games, the Invictus tend to be the Powers that Be. Basically, they always make sure that the rulers are, if not in their pocket, at least ready to lend an open ear to what they have to say. They may not be ruling the Vampires, but they make damn sure that even the most fiery of the Firebrands will have, at some point, to come and ask them to have their powerful friends looking the other way. And they'll do it. For a price.<br /> <br /> A hefty price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T16:36:35-07:00","id":1521084,"title":"","content":"2nd edition seems to have eased up on the idea that Kindred were all stuck in one city; there's the notion of a &quot;cloistered&quot; city where that's still true which implies that the default have more freedom of movement. And the Secrets of the Covenants book definitely portrays the Invictus as being a lot more globally coordinated than I'd previously thought. If you're playing a standard Requiem chronicle that does take place largely in one city than any international Invictus dealings don't really matter unless the players want to get into that sort of thing, though. Still, I'm curious how to balance the Invictus being more decentralized than the Camarilla is in Masquerade but still having them remain so cohesive across the world and across history. Of course there's a good chance that they're lying about how smoothly things have gone for them in the nights since Rome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","user":"Niknokk","date":". 08-20-2023, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-21T10:15:50-07:00","id":1521135,"title":"","content":"I would view it as the Invictus has communication amongst the elders and the Movement is more willing to travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}